/-!
# Cubic-pair word data

The 510 entries cover both orientations of the 255 noncommuting cubic
subgroup pairs with full four-dimensional displacement. Each entry stores
a word of length at most ten, its matrix, its two displacement coefficients,
and the two bounding vectors. These are data only: the separate exhaustive
checker verifies every entry it uses and all 65,536 possible input matrices.

The generator performs ordinary finite binary arithmetic; no generator result
is trusted by Lean. Source application: Aschbacher--Smith E.6.24, p.255.
-/

